erience and improves operational efficiency. Additionally, the increase in the maximum validity of access and ID tokens for OpenID Connect applications from 1 hour to 12 hours has been made [Data: Sources (1986), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 05), (2024, 11, 05))].", "# SAP Cloud Identity Services and Process Automation Overview as of July 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP Cloud Identity Services and Process Automation, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2024.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nSAP Cloud Identity Services has undergone significant updates in 2024, including the introduction of new features and improvements to existing ones. The service now operates with additional IPs in various regions, enhancing its availability and scalability. The ips.application.id property has also been introduced, allowing for better group management and provisioning. These updates demonstrate SAP's commitment to continuously improving its services and meeting the evolving needs of its customers. [Data: Sources (295, 296), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 18), (2024, 07, 18))]\n\n## Process Automation Updates\n\nProcess Automation has also seen significant updates in 2024, including the introduction of new features and improvements to existing ones. The service now supports the Procurement Data Warehouse connector, enabling better data management and integration. The default transformations of Local Identity Directory provisioning systems have also been extended to support the urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:sap:2.0:Group schema, enhancing group management and provisioning. These updates demonstrate SAP's commitment to continuously improving its services and meeting the evolving needs of its customers. [Data: Sources (296, 2590), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 17), (2024, 07, 17))]\n\n## Regional Availability\n\nSAP Cloud Identity Services now operates with additional IPs in various regions, including Brazil, Singapore, South Korea, and Europe (Frankfurt). This enhancement has improved the service's availability and scalability, enabling better support for customers in these regions. [Data: Sources (296, 2586, 2587), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 17), (2024, 07, 17))]", "# Cloud Identity Services and Kyma Runtime Overview as of July 2024\n\nThis report delves into the key components of Cloud Identity Services and Kyma Runtime, highlighting their interactions and updates within the organizational framework. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2024.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP play a pivotal role in managing identity and access management. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential security pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving technological standards. Effective identity management not only prevents security anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (295, 296), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 07, 18))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nKyma Runtime at SAP has been updated to improve its functionality and security. The updates, noted starting mid-2024, are crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational security, especially in managing complex identity and access management systems. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high technological standards and security practices. [Data: Sources (2598, 2599), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 07, 17))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Identity Management\n\nCollaboration between Cloud Identity Services and Kyma Runtime ensures that identity management strategies are technologically sound and that compliance measures consider security risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating identity management with security strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with technological requirements. [Data: Sources (295, 296), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 07, 18))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's technology landscape, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP's operations and development around 2024.\n\n## Business Data Orchestration Updates\n\nBusiness Data Orchestration, a key component of SAP's technology landscape, has undergone significant updates in 2024. The service has been renamed to Business Data Orchestration, and new features have been added, including the ability to display clients and create destinations with client certificate authentication. These updates aim to improve the service's functionality and user experience. [Data: Sources (3204, 3205), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 04, 01))]\n\n## Deprecation of Configure Context and Configure Object ID Behavior Applications\n\nAs of the end of 2025, the applications Configure Context and Configure Object ID Behavior will be deprecated. This change is part of SAP's efforts to streamline its technology landscape and improve customer experience. The applications will remain available for the time being, but newly created roles will no longer include these entries. [Data: Source (211), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 21), (2025, 08, 21))]\n\n## Automation Pilot Enhancements\n\nSAP Automation Pilot has undergone several enhancements in 2025, including the addition of generative AI capabilities, support for the reduce function in dynamic expressions, and new tags for execution status change events. These updates aim to improve the service's functionality and user experience. [Data: Sources (212, 214, 215), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 21), (2025, 08, 21))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP's key components focusing on technology, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold operational standards and manage technological risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## Kyma Runtime Operational Scope\n\nThe Kyma Runtime at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating technological risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential technological pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents technological anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (381, 517), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 04, 03))]\n\n## Joule Module Updates\n\nThe Joule module at SAP BTP has undergone significant updates, including the release of version 1.1.0, which brings the latest version of KEDA (v2.13). This update has improved the browsing experience of Kubernetes resources and enhanced the editing process. Additionally, Joule is now available in the Japan (Tokyo) data center of AWS, and the document grounding capability is now available for Joule integrations. [Data: Sources (258, 360), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 10), (2024, 10, 14))]\n\n## Third-Party Cookies Deprecation\n\nGoogle plans to phase out support for third-party cookies, which will affect non-SAP content, sites that are using a full custom domain, and sites that are using a standalone appRouter. To avoid this situation, customers can apply to participate in the first-party deprecation trial, and request Google to issue them a token that will temporarily re-enable third-party cookies until December 27th, 2024. [Data: Sources (143, 517), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 12, 27))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of April 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance user experience, improve security, and streamline operations. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around April 2024.\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nThe Kyma Runtime at SAP has undergone significant updates, including the release of the Keda module version 1.1.0 and the introduction of new layouts and the Horizon visual theme in the Kyma dashboard. These updates aim to enhance the user experience and improve the browsing experience of Kubernetes resources. Effective updates not only prevent operational anomalies but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (3196, 3197), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 21), (2024, 04, 03))]\n\n## Cloud Portal Service Updates\n\nThe Cloud Portal Service at SAP has introduced several updates, including the deprecation of third-party cookies and the introduction of a first-party deprecation trial. This update aims to improve security and prevent potential access restrictions. Effective updates not only prevent operational anomalies but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (3200, 3201, 3202, 3203), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 04, 03))]\n\n## Business Data Orchestration Updates\n\nThe Business Data Orchestration at SAP has introduced several updates, including the creation of destinations with client certificate authentication and the display of clients. These updates aim to improve the user experience and streamline operations. Effective updates not only prevent operational anomalies but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (3204, 3205), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 01), (2024, 04, 03))]\n\n## Cloud Transport Management Updates\n\nThe Cloud Transport Management at SAP has introduced several updates, including the availability of the service on new data centers and smaller UI changes. These updates aim to improve the user experience and streamline operations. Effective updates not only prevent operational anomalies but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (691, 692), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 06), (2025, 06, 06))]\n\n## Mobile Services Updates\n\nThe Mobile Services at SAP has introduced several updates, including the end of life for Mobile Transaction Bridge and the introduction of device access management. These updates aim to improve security and prevent potential access restrictions. Effective updates not only prevent operational anomalies but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (695, 696), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 05), (2025, 06, 05))]\n\n## SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing Updates\n\nThe SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing at SAP has introduced several updates, including the creation and maintenance of coupons and the configuration of coupon code generation. These updates aim to improve the user experience and streamline operations. Effective updates not only prevent operational anomalies but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (699), Date_Range ((2025, 06, 05), (2025, 06, 05))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold technological standards and manage software risks effectively. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2024.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Runtime Updates\n\nCloud Foundry Runtime has been updated from version 48.5.0 to 48.9.0, with several new features and improvements. This update is crucial for maintaining the stability and security of SAP's cloud infrastructure. Effective updates not only prevent technical anomalies but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (882, 883), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 15), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone Updates\n\nSAP Build Work Zone has been updated with several new features and improvements, including a new navigation system and UX improvements. This update is crucial for maintaining the stability and usability of SAP's software applications. Effective updates not only prevent technical anomalies but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (883, 884), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 15), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## SAP Document AI Updates\n\nSAP Document AI has been updated with several new features and improvements, including overall improvements and support for additional languages. This update is crucial for maintaining the stability and usability of SAP's software applications. Effective updates not only prevent technical anomalies but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (886, 887), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 15), (2025, 05, 15))]", "# SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP Cloud Foundry's key components and services, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide a comprehensive platform for business applications. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Components and Services\n\nSAP BTP Cloud Foundry offers a range of components and services, including SAP Java Buildpack, SAP Task Center, UI5 Flexibility for Key Users, and Edge Integration Cell. These components and services work together to provide a comprehensive platform for business applications, enabling users to develop, deploy, and manage applications efficiently. Effective use of these components and services is crucial for maximizing the benefits of SAP BTP Cloud Foundry and ensuring seamless integration with other SAP systems. [Data: Sources (141, 660), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 06, 27))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between SAP BTP Cloud Foundry's components and services, established in 2024, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP BTP Cloud Foundry. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (141, 660), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 06, 27))]\n\n## SAPUI5 Distribution and Updates\n\nSAPUI5 version 1.124 has been released for UI development and can now be consumed by SAP BTP services. This update provides new features and improvements, enabling users to develop more efficient and effective UI applications. Effective use of SAPUI5 version 1.124 is crucial for maximizing the benefits of SAP BTP Cloud Foundry and ensuring seamless integration with other SAP systems. [Data: Sources (141, 660), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 06, 27))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold technological standards and manage software risks effectively. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2024.\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone Updates\n\nThe SAP Build Work Zone has undergone several updates, including the addition of a new screen in the Site Manager to track the progress of an import process, and the alignment of tile behavior in workpages. These updates aim to improve the user experience and streamline workflows. [Data: Sources (1571, 1572), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 23), (2025, 01, 23))]\n\n## SAP Java Buildpack Updates\n\nThe SAP Java Buildpack has been updated to version 1.109.0 and 2.23.0, with several components updated, including Apache Tomcat, Apache TomEE, and SAP HANA Driver. These updates aim to improve performance and security. [Data: Sources (1572, 