he SAP Java Buildpack has been updated from version 2.23.0 to 2.24.0, adding Apache TomEE 10 and updating several components. This update aims to improve the buildpack's functionality and compatibility with various environments. The update is part of SAP's efforts to enhance its cloud-based services and ensure seamless integration with other SAP products. [Data: Sources (316), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 05), (2025, 02, 20))]\n\n## SAP Start Updates\n\nSAP Start has been updated with new features, including automatic theme detection and theme categorization. These updates aim to improve the user experience and provide a more intuitive interface for users. The updates are part of SAP's efforts to enhance its user interface and ensure a seamless user experience across various platforms. [Data: Sources (317, 318), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 20), (2025, 02, 20))]\n\n## SAPUI5 Distribution Updates\n\nSAPUI5 version 1.133 has been released, providing new features and improvements for UI development. The update aims to enhance the user experience and provide a more intuitive interface for developers. The update is part of SAP's efforts to enhance its UI development tools and ensure seamless integration with other SAP products. [Data: Sources (319), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 20), (2025, 02, 20))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nKyma Runtime has been updated with new features, including improved telemetry and metrics. The update aims to enhance the user experience and provide a more intuitive interface for users. The update is part of SAP's efforts to enhance its cloud-based services and ensure seamless integration with other SAP products. [Data: Sources (320, 321), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 19), (2025, 02, 19))]\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has been updated with new features, including best practices for embedded web pages and known issues for managing data type changes. The update aims to enhance the user experience and provide a more intuitive interface for users. The update is part of SAP's efforts to enhance its automation tools and ensure seamless integration with other SAP products. [Data: Sources (322, 323), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 19), (2025, 02, 19))]\n\n## SAP Datasphere Updates\n\nSAP Datasphere has been updated with new features, including data integration and data modeling. The update aims to enhance the user experience and provide a more intuitive interface for users. The update is part of SAP's efforts to enhance its data management tools and ensure seamless integration with other SAP products. [Data: Sources (324), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 19), (2025, 02, 19))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of September 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around September 2024.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Environment Updates\n\nCloud Foundry, a key environment for SAP's technology components, has seen significant updates in 2024. These updates include the addition of new regions, such as AWS Brazil (São Paulo) and Microsoft Azure Japan (Tokyo), as well as the removal of DSR from SAP Java Buildpack 1 and 2. These changes aim to improve the performance and security of SAP's cloud-based services. [Data: Sources (1, 2), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 30))]\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has seen significant updates in 2024, including the addition of new regions and the enhancement of the user interface. These updates aim to improve the user experience and increase productivity. [Data: Source (4), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 27), (2024, 09, 27))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services has seen significant updates in 2024, including the change in behavior of target transformations and the configuration of security questions and PIN code for password recovery. These updates aim to improve the security and user experience of SAP's cloud-based services. [Data: Sources (5, 6), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 25), (2024, 09, 25))]\n\n## SAP Java Buildpack Updates\n\nSAP Java Buildpack has seen significant updates in 2024, including the removal of DSR and the update of various components. These updates aim to improve the performance and security of SAP's cloud-based services. [Data: Sources (7, 8), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 03), (2024, 09, 19))]\n\n## SAP AI Core Updates\n\nSAP AI Core has seen significant updates in 2024, including the addition of a generative AI hub and the support of additional models from Meta. These updates aim to improve the user experience and increase productivity. [Data: Sources (9, 10, 11, 12), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 16), (2024, 09, 16))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP's key departments focusing on technology, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Operational Scope\n\nCloud Foundry at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in providing a platform for building, deploying, and scaling applications. Their proactive approach helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential application pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective cloud management not only prevents application anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1, 2), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## ABAP Environment and SAPUI5 Version\n\nThe ABAP Environment at SAP BTP ensures that all applications adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on SAPUI5 version 1.120.8, noted starting Q1 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex applications and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (3), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Cloud Foundry and ABAP Environment Departments, established in Q1 2024, ensures that cloud management strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider application risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating cloud management with legal compliance strategies at SAP BTP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (4, 5), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]", "# Cloud Identity Services and Technology Overview as of September 2024\n\nThis report delves into the key components of SAP's Cloud Identity Services and Technology, highlighting their operational scope, core attributes, connections, and noteworthy claims. The information is relevant to the company's operations around September 2024.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP play a pivotal role in managing user identities and access control. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential security risks and ensures continuous compliance with evolving security regulations. Effective identity management not only prevents security breaches but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (2205, 2206), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 25))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Security Enhancements\n\nCloud Identity Services have been upgraded to enhance security features, including password recovery options and SAML 2.0 metadata. These enhancements are crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational security, especially in managing complex user identities and access control. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high security standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (2207, 2208), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 25), (2024, 09, 25))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Security\n\nCollaboration between Cloud Identity Services and other departments, established in 2024, ensures that security measures are integrated with other business strategies. This synergy is vital for holistic security and has been instrumental in aligning SAP's strategies with regulatory requirements. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in maintaining the company's operational stability. [Data: Sources (2209, 2210), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 25), (2024, 09, 25))]", "# Cloud Identity Services Overview as of 2024-09-25\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key components and features of Cloud Identity Services, highlighting their operational scope, recent changes, and notable updates. The information is relevant to the technology landscape as of 2024-09-25.\n\n## Identity Provisioning Operational Scope\n\nThe Identity Provisioning component of Cloud Identity Services is responsible for managing user identities and access to resources. Recent changes, such as the behavior of target transformations that contain a combination of condition and skip operations for updates, have improved the efficiency and accuracy of identity provisioning. Effective identity management is crucial for maintaining the security and integrity of the organization's systems and data. [Data: Sources (748, 2207), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 25))]\n\n## SAP Master Data Integration Changes\n\nResetting the SAP Master Data Integration source system now resets the delta load marker, ensuring consistent behavior with other supported source systems. This change has improved the accuracy and efficiency of identity provisioning and access management. [Data: Sources (2208, 2209), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 25))]\n\n## Security Questions and PIN Code Configuration\n\nThe configuration of security questions and PIN code for password recovery now requires entering Edit mode, enhancing the security and usability of password recovery processes. This change has improved the overall security posture of the organization. [Data: Source (586), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 25))]\n\n## Regular Upgrade of Cloud Identity Services\n\nCloud Identity Services have been upgraded, ensuring that the organization's identity and access management systems remain secure and efficient. This upgrade has improved the overall security and reliability of the organization's systems and data. [Data: Source (2207), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 25))]\n\n## SAML 2.0 Metadata Updates\n\nRecent updates to SAML 2.0 metadata have improved the security and usability of identity and access management processes. Users can now choose which certificate to include in the downloaded tenant SAML 2.0 metadata file, enhancing the flexibility and security of identity management. [Data: Sources (2209, 2210), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 09, 25))]", "# SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Environment Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates as of 2025. The information is relevant to the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment's operations and maintenance.\n\n## SAP Java Buildpack 1 Deprecation and Removal\n\nSAP Java Buildpack 1 has been deprecated and will be removed from the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment on June 30, 2025. This change is necessary to focus efforts on delivering new features, reducing technical debt, and boosting product quality and security. Users are advised to migrate their applications to SAP Java Buildpack 2 as soon as possible. [Data: Sources (286, 323, 1111), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 22), (2025, 04, 03))]\n\n## Cloud Foundry API v2 Deprecation and Removal\n\nThe Cloud Foundry API v2 is deprecated and will be removed from the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment in the first quarter of 2026. Users are advised to migrate their direct usage of CF API v2 to CF API v3. [Data: Sources (195, 871), Date_Range ((2022, 07, 14), (2025, 05, 15))]\n\n## Root Certificate Replacement in the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Environment\n\nThe root certificate authority (CA) used to issue certificates on SAP domains for the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment will be replaced by a newer CA. Users are advised to add the new CA certificate to their trust store to ensure a seamless transition. [Data: Sources (872, 2368), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 18), (2025, 05, 15))]", "# SAP BTP Community Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP community, highlighting key components, their relationships, and notable updates. The information is relevant to the community's operations as of 2025.\n\n## SAP BTP Components and Updates\n\nThe SAP BTP community consists of various components, including SAP Build Process Automation, SAP Document AI, SAP Dynamic Forms, and SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration. These components have undergone significant updates, with new features and improvements added to enhance their functionality and user experience. For instance, SAP Build Process Automation has introduced new content packages, while SAP Document AI has improved its machine learning models for document types such as invoices and purchase orders. These updates demonstrate the community's commitment to innovation and customer satisfaction [Data: Sources (3795, 2082, 2083), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 01), (2024, 10, 22))].\n\n## Kyma Runtime and Kubernetes Upgrades\n\nThe Kyma Runtime environment is planned to be upgraded to Kubernetes 1.33 and 1.32 releases. These upgrades aim to improve the community's operational efficiency and security. The upgrades will be performed in a phased approach, with minimal disruption to workloads. The community recommends ensuring the availability of applications by running multiple replicas across different Availability Zones and configuring Pod Disruption Budgets [Data: Sources (34, 646), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 23), (2025, 10, 17))].\n\n## Authorization and Trust Management Service Updates\n\nThe Authorization and Trust Management Service has undergone updates, including the replacement of the library for JSON Web Tokens (JWT) to improve security and compliance with the OIDC standard. These updates demonstrate the community's commitment to security and customer satisfaction [Data: Sources (35), Date_Range ((2025, 10, 02), (2025, 10, 13))]."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_2986d6645aa5c8be39c427e44f2d8939771bb8016e4f58e1c053c9df78a5ae48_v2"}